<?php
/**
 * Copyright © ElAssal for Trading & Supply. All rights reserved.
 *
 * The `تقييم المنتج` dialog.
 * Figma 1207:30485 (desktop, over the 1207:28688 overlay) / 1204:27392
 * (mobile) — 400 x 574 at BOTH widths, measured, which is why there is no
 * responsive variant of the panel in the stylesheet.
 *
 * The `أترك تقييمك` button that opens it is not here: it belongs to the panel
 * (Figma draws it inside the tab), and it is rendered by review.phtml. This
 * block is moved to page level by the theme's own catalog_product_view.xml —
 * see there for why a dialog cannot live inside a tab panel.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * WHAT THIS REPLACES
 * ===========================================================================
 * Core's form.phtml renders an INLINE form inside the reviews tab, with five
 * fields: a rating, a nickname, a summary, the review text, and a submit. The
 * design has a dialog with three controls — stars, a comment, and a submit —
 * plus a dismiss. So:
 *
 *   nickname   supplied server-side from the signed-in customer's first name
 *   title      derived server-side from the opening of the comment
 *
 * both by Spartrak\Review\Plugin\Review\SupplyFieldsFigmaDoesNotCollect, which
 * carries the full reasoning for each. Magento's own Review::validate() refuses
 * a review without them and both columns are NOT NULL, so they are supplied
 * rather than dropped — the alternative was adding two fields the design does
 * not have, or forking core's validation.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * A NATIVE <dialog>, NOT Magento_Ui/js/modal
 * ===========================================================================
 * The platform's modal component is what components/_modal.less already
 * restyles, and it was the first candidate. `<dialog>` wins here on the terms
 * CLAUDE.md section 13 sets out, because the BROWSER already implements what
 * that component ships JavaScript to do: the top layer (so nothing can stack
 * over it), the ::backdrop scrim, Escape to dismiss, focus containment, and
 * making the rest of the page inert. Reaching for the component would have
 * meant loading Magento_Ui's modal, jQuery UI dialog and the underscore
 * templates it depends on, to reproduce behaviour that is already native.
 *
 * What is left for JavaScript is opening it, and one line of validation
 * presentation — see js/spartrak-review-dialog.js.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * THE FORM POSTS. IT DOES NOT NEED JAVASCRIPT TO WORK.
 * ===========================================================================
 * A plain multipart-less POST to core's own `review/product/post`, with core's
 * own form key, core's own rating option ids and core's own field names. With
 * JavaScript off the dialog cannot be opened by the CTA — but the form inside
 * it is still a real form, native constraint validation still refuses an empty
 * comment, and the server still validates everything again. Nothing about the
 * submission depends on the enhancement.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * THE TWO EXTENSION CONTAINERS ARE RENDERED
 * ===========================================================================
 * `form_fields_before` and `form_additional_review_info` are core's slots and
 * they are NOT decoration: Magento_ReCaptchaReview injects its widget into the
 * second one. Dropping them would leave the captcha unrendered, the token
 * absent, and every review rejected server-side by a validator the shopper
 * cannot see.
 *
 * @var \Magento\Review\Block\Form $block
 * @var \Magento\Framework\Escaper $escaper
 */

$canWrite = (bool) $block->getAllowWriteReviewFlag();
$ratings = $block->getRatings();
$dimensions = $ratings && $ratings->getSize() ? $ratings : [];
// Figma draws ONE row of five stars, which is the single-rating-dimension
// store this design was made for. Magento allows several (Quality, Value,
// Price side by side), and a second one would otherwise be silently dropped —
// leaving a configured rating with no votes and a histogram that disagrees with
// the admin. So each active dimension gets its own control, and when there is
// exactly one the result is the Figma frame unchanged.
$isSingleDimension = is_object($dimensions) && $dimensions->getSize() === 1;

if (!$canWrite) {
    // A signed-out shopper on a store that does not allow guest reviews gets
    // no dialog at all — the panel's CTA opens the sign-in modal instead. See
    // ViewModel\ProductReviews::canWriteReview() and review.phtml.
    return;
}
?>
<dialog id="spartrak-review-dialog"
        class="spartrak-review-dialog"
        aria-labelledby="spartrak-review-dialog-title"
        data-mage-init='<?= $escaper->escapeHtmlAttr(json_encode([
            'spartrakReviewDialog' => [
                // Magento's own rating summary in the product info column links
                // to `#review-form`, which core renders and this design does
                // not. Listed here so that link opens the dialog rather than
                // jumping to an anchor that no longer exists.
                'externalTriggers' => '.product-reviews-summary .action.add',
            ],
        ])) ?>'>
    <form class="spartrak-review-dialog__panel"
          action="<?= $escaper->escapeUrl($block->getAction()) ?>"
          method="post"
          id="spartrak-review-form">
        <?= $block->getBlockHtml('formkey') ?>
        <?= $block->getChildHtml('form_fields_before') ?>

        <div class="spartrak-review-dialog__header">
            <h2 class="spartrak-review-dialog__title" id="spartrak-review-dialog-title">
                <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Rate this product')) ?>
            </h2>
            <button type="button"
                    class="spartrak-review-dialog__close"
                    data-review-dialog-close
                    aria-label="<?= $escaper->escapeHtmlAttr(__('Close')) ?>"></button>
        </div>

        <div class="spartrak-review-dialog__content">
            <div class="spartrak-review-dialog__group">
                <?php foreach ($dimensions as $dimension): ?>
                    <?php
                    $groupId = 'spartrak-review-rating-' . (int) $dimension->getId();
                    $promptId = $groupId . '-prompt';
                    // getOptions() is a plain array once the collection has run
                    // addOptionToItems(); counted once so the accessible name of
                    // each star can say "3 of 5" without asking five times.
                    $options = $dimension->getOptions() ?: [];
                    $optionCount = count($options);
                    ?>
                    <?php /*
                      role="radiogroup" and not <fieldset><legend>, because
                      Figma puts the prompt BELOW the stars (stars at y=36.6,
                      the question at y=102.4 of the 180px box) and a <legend>
                      is only the accessible name of a fieldset when it is that
                      fieldset's FIRST child. The alternatives were a hidden
                      legend duplicating the visible question — two copies of
                      one string to keep in step — or CSS reordering a <legend>,
                      whose rendering is inconsistent inside a flex container.
                      This names the group once, from the text the shopper can
                      actually see (CLAUDE.md section 15: ARIA to fill a
                      genuine gap).
                    */ ?>
                    <div class="spartrak-review-dialog__rating"
                         role="radiogroup"
                         aria-labelledby="<?= $escaper->escapeHtmlAttr($promptId) ?>">
                        <div class="spartrak-review-dialog__stars">
                            <?php foreach ($options as $option): ?>
                                <?php
                                $inputId = $groupId . '-' . (int) $option->getValue();
                                ?>
                                <input class="spartrak-review-dialog__star-input"
                                       type="radio"
                                       id="<?= $escaper->escapeHtmlAttr($inputId) ?>"
                                       name="ratings[<?= $escaper->escapeHtmlAttr($dimension->getId()) ?>]"
                                       value="<?= $escaper->escapeHtmlAttr($option->getId()) ?>"
                                       required>
                                <label class="spartrak-review-dialog__star"
                                       for="<?= $escaper->escapeHtmlAttr($inputId) ?>">
                                    <span class="spartrak-visually-hidden"><?= $escaper->escapeHtml(
                                        __('Rating %1 of %2', (int) $option->getValue(), $optionCount)
                                    ) ?></span>
                                </label>
                            <?php endforeach; ?>
                        </div>

                        <p class="spartrak-review-dialog__prompt" id="<?= $escaper->escapeHtmlAttr($promptId) ?>">
                            <?php /*
                              One dimension: the design's own question. More
                              than one: that dimension's own name, because
                              "what is your rating?" five times over names
                              nothing.
                            */ ?>
                            <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(
                                $isSingleDimension
                                    ? __('How would you rate this product?')
                                    : __($dimension->getRatingCode())
                            ) ?>
                        </p>
                    </div>
                <?php endforeach; ?>

                <div class="spartrak-review-dialog__field">
                    <label class="spartrak-review-dialog__label" for="spartrak-review-detail">
                        <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Your comment on the product')) ?>
                    </label>
                    <textarea class="spartrak-review-dialog__input"
                              id="spartrak-review-detail"
                              name="detail"
                              rows="3"
                              required
                              aria-describedby="spartrak-review-detail-error"></textarea>
                    <?php /*
                      The design's own error slot — the "Hint Error" frame in
                      the mobile dialog (1204:27430), drawn but switched off.
                      Rendered empty and hidden; js/spartrak-review-dialog.js
                      fills it from the browser's own constraint validation, so
                      the message is native and the presentation is Figma's.
                      role="alert" so it is announced when it appears.
                    */ ?>
                    <p class="spartrak-review-dialog__hint"
                       id="spartrak-review-detail-error"
                       data-review-dialog-error
                       role="alert"
                       hidden>
                        <span class="spartrak-review-dialog__hint-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <span class="spartrak-review-dialog__hint-text"></span>
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <?= $block->getChildHtml('form_additional_review_info') ?>

            <div class="spartrak-review-dialog__actions">
                <button type="submit" class="spartrak-review-dialog__submit">
                    <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Leave your comment')) ?>
                </button>
                <?php /*
                  `متابعة التسوق` is an <a> in the frame, and it is a BUTTON
                  here. Figma gives it no destination, and the only honest
                  reading of "continue shopping" from a dialog on the page the
                  shopper is already shopping on is "close this" — inventing a
                  URL for it would send them somewhere the design never asked
                  for.
                */ ?>
                <button type="button"
                        class="spartrak-review-dialog__dismiss"
                        data-review-dialog-close>
                    <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Continue shopping')) ?>
                </button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </form>
</dialog>
